  "substantive_research": [
    "Prior primary1910arrangement/1911Belgian law and1965StateDepartment IBS51 establish historical median-line context. The1965position uncertainty is dated to materials reviewed then; it is not a current legal-status finding. These retained reads are reused with their scope limits, not rerun or claimed newly performed.",
    "AU2017/2018records establish technical process. ActualAU2022page records four-state shoreline digitization for eventual median determination. Actual2026newsletterpage17 records25–27March2026Lusaka review of a draftMoU and reaffirmation agenda; no adopted coordinate product confirmed in the passage. LakeKariba buoy pilot on samepage is notTanganyika.",
    "Exact TZAADM1original archive, DBF/XML/license and earlier4.0version inspected.2015represented source is OSM/Wambacher;2017attributeprocessing is not survey date. Original threefieldDBF has no OSMrelation/version/exportsettings. Exporter2019documented optional land clipping but historical selected setting remains unknown; lake relation1374224is a clipping input, not an administrative median relation.",
    "COD2019original target archive explicitly documents OCHAatlas digitization, watercourse splitting, topology/naming/IMWG checks and later field changes. It supplies no exact lake median, target-specific atlas sheet/control points or rule proving that a lake edge was reconstructed. Watercourse splitting is not assumed to construct lake medians.",
    "Fizi original two keys are water-classified and both now have only Kigoma negative8 / feature16 interior scan membership. Burundi eight original operands are each explicitly empty under the native predicate.",
    "ActualBurundi2015laws establish commune regrouping while retaining delimitations and administrative functions. That completed research is retained as context; it is not required to resolve an absentBDInative contact and cannot supply the activeKigoma lake line."
  ],
  "unresolved_question": "Whether the original2015Kigoma administrative lake edge is spatially applicable against CODFizi at these two native centres. Administrative water jurisdiction is possible, but neither water classification nor a source polygon by itself adjudicates it.",
  "reasonable_failed_steps_and_genuine_limits": [
    "HistoricalTZAexportsettings/OSMrelationversion not recoverable from exact original and earlier archive inspected.",
    "No adopted spatial line exposed by the actualAU2022/2026records inspected; not a claim that no agreement exists."
  ],
  "case_limits": [
    "EarlierBDIpublication access obstacles remain real but are not pending blockers for these two activeKigoma contacts.",
    "No boundary tie is reported at either key; interior alone is stock scan membership, not proof of full-cell geographic intersection."
  ],
  "sufficiency_judgment": "Substantive source-specific research and the historical/modern primary boundary inquiry support a bounded researched-unresolved proposal for these exact2. No positive territory interpretation or removal of the original veto is justified.",
  "native_semantics": "interior means stock centre-sampled scan-span membership; all these keys have no namedtie. Empty kinds means no native-predicate contact, not no geometric area overlap or legal inapplicability. Entire originaloperand list and hashes remain below.",
